(994708, 117129, 27440, '<td valign="top">What I like:<br/>- an interesting formation of branches and leaves<br/>- I think I see the face<br/>What I dislike:<br/>-The tilt, seems to be contrary to the calmness of a tree :)<br/>-The colours, well if the light was so bright and there was no way you could enhance the colours by a different angle or tie of exposure or a filter or ps, then you should show us this. I undestand that b&amp;2 would "hide" the tree, but maybe selective desat? I read on the forum that there is a way to do it and it still would be within the rules.<br/> <br/>I give you a 5, why? There are shots of tree faces in this chalange that are better.<br/>Don''t give up, shoot and experiment :)</td>', 'What I like:- an interesting formation of branches and leaves- I think I see the faceWhat I dislike:-The tilt, seems to be contrary to the calmness of a tree :)-The colours, well if the light was so bright and there was no way you could enhance the colours by a different angle or tie of exposure or a filter or ps, then you should show us this. I undestand that b&2 would "hide" the tree, but maybe selective desat? I read on the forum that there is a way to do it and it still would be within the rules. I give you a 5, why? There are shots of tree faces in this chalange that are better.Don''t give up, shoot and experiment :)', '2004-11-06 03:29:56.000000', NULL, 1),
(994714, 117464, 27440, '<td valign="top">What I like:<br/>-An unusual, some may say bizzare subject.<br/>-Creative ( thinking of this shell )<br/>-The way he is ''lit through''<br/>-Great oportunities this subject gives<br/>What I dislike:<br/>-The background is terrbile. If you wanted a backlight maybe a paper box painted in black with a torch covered with crepe paper would do the tric.<br/>-Such a subject such oportunities, and well sorry but all wasted.<br/> <br/>I give you a 5, why? I wrote :) ( don''t be mad at me, just think what you could do better )<br/>Maybe putting this feller in a thick but to the ground layer of smoke? Youdrill a whole in a bottle put a rolled paper in it  but not horizontally. The end that you will light must be higher, and from the other side the smoke will come out in a condensed form - not willing to spread - like a fog. Then you put this buggie into this smoke and backlight him with soft and warm light. Torch covered with thick red paper would do. This would even emphasise the bizzarness or unusuality.</td>', 'What I like:-An unusual, some may say bizzare subject.-Creative ( thinking of this shell )-The way he is ''lit through''-Great oportunities this subject givesWhat I dislike:-The background is terrbile. If you wanted a backlight maybe a paper box painted in black with a torch covered with crepe paper would do the tric.-Such a subject such oportunities, and well sorry but all wasted. I give you a 5, why? I wrote :) ( don''t be mad at me, just think what you could do better )Maybe putting this feller in a thick but to the ground layer of smoke? Youdrill a whole in a bottle put a rolled paper in it  but not horizontally. The end that you will light must be higher, and from the other side the smoke will come out in a condensed form - not willing to spread - like a fog. Then you put this buggie into this smoke and backlight him with soft and warm light. Torch covered with thick red paper would do. This would even emphasise the bizzarness or unusuality.', '2004-11-06 03:37:49.000000', NULL, 1),
