(996318, 118107, 27440, '<td valign="top">What I like :<br/> <br/>-Good capture<br/>-the claws are nice<br/>-I know how difficult it is to shoot an animal.<br/> <br/>What I dislike:<br/>-The leaf should go<br/>-The details of the screw should go<br/>- The string somehow destroys the composition. I see rather chaos ( but that might be your intention). It might be a good thing because you might see it as adding to the danger and fighting  situation<br/>- I am not sure about the DOF you used<br/>-As I understand the claw was the subject, since the cat held his other leg so far in front the placing is ok, but if possible you could have moved it a bit to the right(the claw that is). A smaller DOF would have enhanced the claw. If selective saturatiob/desaturation was permitted, the claws them selves could be in colour but the rest in b&amp;w.<br/>-The colours seem to be so ...dead, and it somehow mismatches the spirit in these claws of the cat. B&amp;w might repair this.<br/> <br/>All in all I give you a 5 , but close to a 6. Why? Partaly I wrote, but also because the competition is better.<br/> <br/>Good luck and go get them  :) Think more of the part of the photos that could give a meaning to the photograph, think out of the box, Don''t just limit your self to an interesting capture, even in an interesting capture thing''s might add to the overall ouctome. Think of those ''things''<br/></td>', 'What I like : -Good capture-the claws are nice-I know how difficult it is to shoot an animal. What I dislike:-The leaf should go-The details of the screw should go- The string somehow destroys the composition. I see rather chaos ( but that might be your intention). It might be a good thing because you might see it as adding to the danger and fighting  situation- I am not sure about the DOF you used-As I understand the claw was the subject, since the cat held his other leg so far in front the placing is ok, but if possible you could have moved it a bit to the right(the claw that is). A smaller DOF would have enhanced the claw. If selective saturatiob/desaturation was permitted, the claws them selves could be in colour but the rest in b&w.-The colours seem to be so ...dead, and it somehow mismatches the spirit in these claws of the cat. B&w might repair this. All in all I give you a 5 , but close to a 6. Why? Partaly I wrote, but also because the competition is better. Good luck and go get them  :) Think more of the part of the photos that could give a meaning to the photograph, think out of the box, Don''t just limit your self to an interesting capture, even in an interesting capture thing''s might add to the overall ouctome. Think of those ''things''', '2004-11-07 03:52:14.000000', NULL, 1),
(996385, 118033, 10212, '<td valign="top">Brilliant sense of humour behind this one. Might not have anything to do with nature per se but you get a nine from me!</td>', 'Brilliant sense of humour behind this one. Might not have anything to do with nature per se but you get a nine from me!', '2004-11-07 05:57:22.000000', NULL, 1),
