(1005628, 118018, 27306, '<td valign="top">Thanks for all your comments. You gave me a good deal of positive stimulation.<br/>p.s. The bellpepper fell victim to breakfast. We felt really sorry for it :-)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-11 07:31:50.</i></td>', 'Thanks for all your comments. You gave me a good deal of positive stimulation.p.s. The bellpepper fell victim to breakfast. We felt really sorry for it :-)', '2004-11-11 07:30:59.000000', '2004-11-11 07:31:50.000000', 0),
(1005746, 116658, 28339, '<td valign="top">Definitely amazing. <br/>But ''The Amazing Tranquility'' would better suit as a title than ''The Amazing Silence''</td>', 'Definitely amazing. But ''The Amazing Tranquility'' would better suit as a title than ''The Amazing Silence''', '2004-11-11 09:05:21.000000', NULL, 0),
(1006066, 117194, 19672, '<td valign="top">Thanks all, this was an experiment and my first night shoot...<br/> <br/>Not happy, still learning, but i thought i''d post and share.<br/> <br/>It was nearly impossible to get all objects in focus and proper lighting.  I had to use a second curtain affect to get the reed to show up at all. It was still to bright so I need to learn how to adjust more.<br/> <br/>I realized afterwards that my polarizer lens might have helped even though it''s not the typical sunny day use.<br/> <br/>Yes the reed was blurring...<br/> <br/>I was getting a bit closer to what I wanted but a fog rolled in making all shots blurry irregardless of focused or not.  This was VERY challenging.<br/> <br/>I''d rate it a 40% score in my personal book. But I think it still shows my "eye" for a good shot. Just not my technical knowledge to make the shot.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Thanks all, this was an experiment and my first night shoot... Not happy, still learning, but i thought i''d post and share. It was nearly impossible to get all objects in focus and proper lighting.  I had to use a second curtain affect to get the reed to show up at all. It was still to bright so I need to learn how to adjust more. I realized afterwards that my polarizer lens might have helped even though it''s not the typical sunny day use. Yes the reed was blurring... I was getting a bit closer to what I wanted but a fog rolled in making all shots blurry irregardless of focused or not.  This was VERY challenging. I''d rate it a 40% score in my personal book. But I think it still shows my "eye" for a good shot. Just not my technical knowledge to make the shot. ', '2004-11-11 12:13:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1006319, 116418, 14812, '<td valign="top">Awesome shot, and it meets the challenge so well. Thanks for showing us this perspective, and so nicely done too :).</td>', 'Awesome shot, and it meets the challenge so well. Thanks for showing us this perspective, and so nicely done too :).', '2004-11-11 14:51:13.000000', NULL, 0),
