(1012535, 118034, 28337, '<td valign="top">Thanks for your comments everyone. I would like to know what you think of this picture outside the challenge. (I do realize its not very bizarre).</td>', 'Thanks for your comments everyone. I would like to know what you think of this picture outside the challenge. (I do realize its not very bizarre).', '2004-11-15 19:32:20.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013220, 117821, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>Others have already pointed out that you could have used more Depth of field. This might have been hard due to light, might not have had a tripod with you, and even if you did the bug would move and would be blurry. Try shooting at least with a 1/125 shutter, see if that gives you alittle more aperature to work with. You can also bump your ISO up to get more, but that will make it that much more grainy. You have to give and take. Personaly I would have liked to see his face. Other than that good attempt.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-16 14:39:01.</i></td>', '::Critique Club:: Others have already pointed out that you could have used more Depth of field. This might have been hard due to light, might not have had a tripod with you, and even if you did the bug would move and would be blurry. Try shooting at least with a 1/125 shutter, see if that gives you alittle more aperature to work with. You can also bump your ISO up to get more, but that will make it that much more grainy. You have to give and take. Personaly I would have liked to see his face. Other than that good attempt.', '2004-11-16 05:14:32.000000', '2004-11-16 14:39:01.000000', 0),
(1013225, 117970, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>Like Riggs said you have a good eye to see this as you were walking along. The photo looks great. Wonder what it looks like with a verticle shot. Keep it up.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-16 14:39:34.</i></td>', '::Critique Club:: Like Riggs said you have a good eye to see this as you were walking along. The photo looks great. Wonder what it looks like with a verticle shot. Keep it up.', '2004-11-16 05:19:24.000000', '2004-11-16 14:39:34.000000', 0),
(1013230, 117062, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>It''s hard to take a photo of the moon unless you have the right equipment. Looks like you did a pretty good job, it''s just there aren''t that many ways the moon can be shot and if the photo isn''t absolutely sharp it will be hard to stand out. I commend you on the attempt.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-16 14:40:28.</i></td>', '::Critique Club:: It''s hard to take a photo of the moon unless you have the right equipment. Looks like you did a pretty good job, it''s just there aren''t that many ways the moon can be shot and if the photo isn''t absolutely sharp it will be hard to stand out. I commend you on the attempt.', '2004-11-16 05:24:15.000000', '2004-11-16 14:40:28.000000', 0),
(1013234, 117727, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>Pretty picture. Might could have used a bit more aperture to make it more crisp, or maybe when you sized it for DPC you should have sharpened it a bit. Another thing that probably hurt you was that there is not much about the pic that makes it bizarre, even though it looks to be a very pretty place.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2004-11-16 14:40:47.</i></td>', '::Critique Club:: Pretty picture. Might could have used a bit more aperture to make it more crisp, or maybe when you sized it for DPC you should have sharpened it a bit. Another thing that probably hurt you was that there is not much about the pic that makes it bizarre, even though it looks to be a very pretty place.', '2004-11-16 05:27:59.000000', '2004-11-16 14:40:47.000000', 0),
(1013237, 116658, 15926, '<td valign="top">Beautiful shot, gratz on the ribbon.</td>', 'Beautiful shot, gratz on the ribbon.', '2004-11-16 05:33:44.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013343, 118150, 23535, '<td valign="top">wow... great pic... congrats..</td>', 'wow... great pic... congrats..', '2004-11-16 08:21:07.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013352, 117967, 15397, '<td valign="top">hahaha... I really did fall assleep.. kewl :)</td>', 'hahaha... I really did fall assleep.. kewl :)', '2004-11-16 08:35:35.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013354, 118150, 27771, '<td valign="top">Your description of this photo reminded me of things I used to say when I was working in Wisconsin for a summer, years ago. The skies there are so magnificent, and down here in Illinois, I don''t get much chance to observe beautiful skies. So when I get the chance like that, I too stop and wonder. I''ve forgotten how much I enjoy just stopping and being amazed by our skies.<br/> <br/>Thanks for the image and the flashback.</td>', 'Your description of this photo reminded me of things I used to say when I was working in Wisconsin for a summer, years ago. The skies there are so magnificent, and down here in Illinois, I don''t get much chance to observe beautiful skies. So when I get the chance like that, I too stop and wonder. I''ve forgotten how much I enjoy just stopping and being amazed by our skies. Thanks for the image and the flashback.', '2004-11-16 08:36:29.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013565, 117023, 24931, '<td valign="top">Thank you everyone.<br/> <br/>I think that cropping <i>could</i> benefit this, depending on what you were going for. I was trying to make the flower seem small, even if there was really nothing to compare to.<br/> <br/>I would have loved to get closer to this interesting...thing, but with my current camera set-up, this was about as close as I could get. Maybe I should buy a close up lens ;)<br/> <br/>Thanks again,<br/>-Tristan</td>', 'Thank you everyone. I think that cropping could benefit this, depending on what you were going for. I was trying to make the flower seem small, even if there was really nothing to compare to. I would have loved to get closer to this interesting...thing, but with my current camera set-up, this was about as close as I could get. Maybe I should buy a close up lens ;) Thanks again,-Tristan', '2004-11-16 12:11:24.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013641, 117662, 27845, '<td valign="top">Aw, I hoped you''d get a ribbon. I love it more everytime I have a look at it...</td>', 'Aw, I hoped you''d get a ribbon. I love it more everytime I have a look at it...', '2004-11-16 13:08:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013762, 118139, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>This is a well done photo, detail on the geese is good. The stick in the background is a bit distracting. As for bizarre I think it suffered there too. Some people probably didn''t take the time to understand two animals being together for life is a bit bizarre. Nice try on the challenge and good picture. <br/></td>', '::Critique Club:: This is a well done photo, detail on the geese is good. The stick in the background is a bit distracting. As for bizarre I think it suffered there too. Some people probably didn''t take the time to understand two animals being together for life is a bit bizarre. Nice try on the challenge and good picture. ', '2004-11-16 14:38:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013786, 116940, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>You did find some bizarre produce. I''m split on the shadows. In one hand they are a bit distracting, but when you look closer you can actually see the bird better in the shadow, especially on the "penguin". Love the colors. I think you should have used a higher aperture to make them a little more crisp. Other than that great find and pic.</td>', '::Critique Club:: You did find some bizarre produce. I''m split on the shadows. In one hand they are a bit distracting, but when you look closer you can actually see the bird better in the shadow, especially on the "penguin". Love the colors. I think you should have used a higher aperture to make them a little more crisp. Other than that great find and pic.', '2004-11-16 14:49:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(1013791, 117464, 17148, '<td valign="top">::Critique Club::<br/> <br/>This is a very strange picture. I like it. Maybe tilting the camera to get less of the tree that just looks black in the bottom left would have been better. The lighting looks a tad dark on his bottom half but I think you did a good job keeping your subject and the background together. Nice job finding this.</td>', '::Critique Club:: This is a very strange picture. I like it. Maybe tilting the camera to get less of the tree that just looks black in the bottom left would have been better. The lighting looks a tad dark on his bottom half but I think you did a good job keeping your subject and the background together. Nice job finding this.', '2004-11-16 14:56:28.000000', NULL, 0),
(1014387, 118150, 201, '<td valign="top">Congrats! What a great photo. I too travel with my camera every day. I hope only I''m as fortunant to capture such a great sunset like that. Thank You for sharing it with us.</td>', 'Congrats! What a great photo. I too travel with my camera every day. I hope only I''m as fortunant to capture such a great sunset like that. Thank You for sharing it with us.', '2004-11-16 21:01:15.000000', NULL, 0),
(1017021, 117676, 23913, '<td valign="top">i was going through the bizarre nature finals once more and and saw this for the 2 since voting just wanted to say it is well done and u should be proud as it is your 1st entry and u got top 30.<br/> <br/>way to go on a great shot.</td>', 'i was going through the bizarre nature finals once more and and saw this for the 2 since voting just wanted to say it is well done and u should be proud as it is your 1st entry and u got top 30. way to go on a great shot.', '2004-11-17 14:39:40.000000', NULL, 0),
(1021903, 116805, 27161, '<td valign="top">Bizarreness is pretty subjective.  I guess my pic was riding the line.  The pic does have those resolution lines.  I realized them too late.  I used the Microsoft picture editor to shrink the picture.  I won''t make that mistake again.</td>', 'Bizarreness is pretty subjective.  I guess my pic was riding the line.  The pic does have those resolution lines.  I realized them too late.  I used the Microsoft picture editor to shrink the picture.  I won''t make that mistake again.', '2004-11-19 10:07:00.000000', NULL, 0),
