(1713748, 117428, 14986, '<td valign="top">I really like the shapes and assortment of colors and patterns in the shot.  It almost looks like wrapping paper or the like, with the whole frame filled up.  Maybe it wasn''t bizarre enough for some folks, because I don''t see why this would score anything below a 6.   I like it!</td>', 'I really like the shapes and assortment of colors and patterns in the shot.  It almost looks like wrapping paper or the like, with the whole frame filled up.  Maybe it wasn''t bizarre enough for some folks, because I don''t see why this would score anything below a 6.   I like it!', '2005-09-16 09:53:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(1755923, 117428, 30861, '<td valign="top">Vastly underrated image, this. It fell prey to the DPC mindset that an image has to have a focal point to be "good". This is a shot wherein everything int he frame is the "subject" and no one element stands out, and it''s very well done IMO. In the "landscape/natural light" mentorship thread we recently touched on this approach; our "assignment" was "Landscape Without Subject".<br/> <br/>Robt.</td>', 'Vastly underrated image, this. It fell prey to the DPC mindset that an image has to have a focal point to be "good". This is a shot wherein everything int he frame is the "subject" and no one element stands out, and it''s very well done IMO. In the "landscape/natural light" mentorship thread we recently touched on this approach; our "assignment" was "Landscape Without Subject". Robt.', '2005-10-03 14:46:55.000000', NULL, 0),
